---
import ChapterOrnament from './ChapterOrnament.astro';
---
<section class="model-overview" id="what-is-a-semantic-layer" aria-labelledby="model-overview-heading">
  <ChapterOrnament section="executable-definitions" />
  <h2 id="model-overview-heading">Put the definition in the model. Reuse it in each query.</h2>
  <div class="definition-callout">
    <p><strong>A semantic layer is a shared specification for business metrics and the rules for using them.</strong></p>
    <p>Crossfield makes that specification executable in DuckDB, so reporting definitions can be maintained and reviewed independently of individual reports.</p>
  </div>
  <figure class="model-path" aria-label="Define the reporting rules, attach the semantic model, then query and validate in DuckDB">
    <ol>
      <li><span class="step-number qf-figure" aria-hidden="true">1</span><h3>Define the reporting rules.</h3><p>Specify the calculations, which records count, and how sources can be combined.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number qf-figure" aria-hidden="true">2</span><h3>Attach the model.</h3><p>Make those definitions a named catalog alongside the data in your DuckDB connection.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step-number qf-figure" aria-hidden="true">3</span><h3>Query and validate.</h3><p>Select metrics and dimensions. Crossfield checks the request; DuckDB executes it.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <figcaption>The model retains the reporting rules as users ask different questions. Optional strict mode rejects supported queries that bypass those rules.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
<style>
  .model-overview { padding-block:3.5rem; margin-top:3rem; scroll-margin-top:9rem; }
  h2 { max-width:28ch; margin:0; font-size:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3rem); line-height:1.15; }
  .definition-callout { margin-top:1.75rem; max-width:960px; padding:clamp(1.25rem,3vw,1.75rem); border:1px solid var(--color-soil-300); border-left:4px solid var(--color-field-700); border-radius:.25rem; background:var(--color-soil-100); }
  .definition-callout p { margin:0; font-size:1.0625rem; line-height:1.75; }
  .definition-callout strong { font-size:1.125rem; font-weight:600; }
  .definition-callout p + p { margin-top:.85rem; color:var(--color-soil-700); }
  .model-path { margin:2.5rem 0 0; }
  ol { display:grid; gap:1.75rem; padding:0; list-style:none; }
  li { position:relative; min-width:0; padding-top:1.2rem; border-top:2px solid var(--color-field-700); }
  .step-number { display:grid; place-items:center; width:2.4rem; height:2.4rem; border:1px solid var(--color-field-700); border-radius:50%; background:#f0f3e9; color:var(--color-field-700); }
  h3 { margin-top:1rem; font-size:1.4rem; line-height:1.3; }
  li p,figcaption { color:var(--color-soil-700); font-size:.9375rem; line-height:1.8; }
  li p { margin-top:.7rem; }
  figcaption { margin-top:1.5rem; font-size:.8125rem; }
  @media(min-width:768px) { ol { grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:2.5rem; } li:not(:last-child)::after { content:'→'; position:absolute; right:-1.75rem; top:1.5rem; color:var(--color-field-700); font-size:1.25rem; } }
  @media(max-width:640px) { .model-overview { padding-block:2.5rem; margin-top:1.5rem; } }
</style>
